WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.687 --> 00:00:16.467
we walked toward St.

2
00:00:16.487 --> 00:00:21.291
Luke's College in the twilight, Holmes questioned Soames about who might have known the proofs were in his

3
00:00:21.331 --> 00:00:24.394
room. "Did you have any visitors after the proofs arrived?"

4
00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:25.395
Holmes asked.

5
00:00:25.415 --> 00:00:26.716
"Only one.

6
00:00:27.197 --> 00:00:30.900
Daulat Ras is an Indian student who's taking the exam," Soames said.

7
00:00:31.648 --> 00:00:34.730
"He lives two floors above me and had a quick question about the exam."

8
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.472
"Hmm." Holmes thought for a moment.

9
00:00:37.492 --> 00:00:40.914
"Is it possible he recognized the papers on your desk as proofs?"

10
00:00:41.994 --> 00:00:42.675
"Probably not.

11
00:00:43.055 --> 00:00:45.877
They were still rolled up because I hadn't started reading them yet."

12
00:00:46.717 --> 00:00:48.518
"Hmm," Holmes said again.

13
00:00:48.538 --> 00:00:50.319
"What about Bannister?

14
00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.301
Could he have known about the proofs before he entered your rooms?"

15
00:00:54.162 --> 00:00:55.182
Soames thought for a moment.

16
00:00:55.963 --> 00:00:57.464
"He's worked at the college for many years.

17
00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:03.003
"So, he's probably aware that they arrive the day before the exam starts.

18
00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.184
But he's quite busy with other things.

19
00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:07.306
I doubt he knew they were there."

20
00:01:07.326 --> 00:01:13.810
"I think we'll find that whoever copied the proofs came upon them accidentally, and—" Holmes paused dramatically.

21
00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.491
"It was a student."

22
00:01:15.512 --> 00:01:16.932
"Oh, dear."

23
00:01:17.673 --> 00:01:20.295
Soames removed his hat and ran a nervous hand through his hair.

24
00:01:20.895 --> 00:01:22.516
We walked through the main gates of St.

25
00:01:22.556 --> 00:01:24.037
Luke's and entered a large courtyard.

26
00:01:24.798 --> 00:01:27.420
Soames pointed out his rooms, which were on the ground floor.

27
00:01:28.104 --> 00:01:31.547
Next to his windows, an arched doorway led to a worn stone staircase.

28
00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:33.689
"How many students live above you?"

29
00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:34.690
Holmes asked.

30
00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.072
"Just three."

31
00:01:36.552 --> 00:01:38.054
Soames proceeded to tell us about them.

32
00:01:38.754 --> 00:01:40.776
Richard Gilchrist lived on the floor above Soames.

33
00:01:42.878 --> 00:01:45.981
A scholar and athlete, he was on the college rugby and cricket teams.

34
00:01:46.802 --> 00:01:50.125
He also competed in hurdles and long jump for the track and field team.

35
00:01:50.986 --> 00:01:52.988
"You may have heard of his father," Soames said.

36
00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:57.933
"The senior Gilchrist was in the news because he spent all the family money before he died."

37
00:01:57.953 --> 00:02:01.034
"I do recall something about that," I said.

38
00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:04.335
"Young Gilchrist was left almost penniless, as I remember."

39
00:02:04.355 --> 00:02:09.256
"That's correct, but I think Gilchrist will do well in life because he's a hard worker."

40
00:02:09.956 --> 00:02:12.357
Soames continued describing the students who lived above him.

41
00:02:13.017 --> 00:02:15.818
Daulat Ras' room was above Gilchrist's, on the next floor.

42
00:02:16.618 --> 00:02:18.739
He was a quiet student, steady and methodical.

43
00:02:19.379 --> 00:02:23.080
Although he got good grades, Ras believed Greek was his weakest subject.

44
00:02:25.216 --> 00:02:27.077
Miles McLaren lived on the top floor.

45
00:02:27.757 --> 00:02:31.318
He was a brilliant student when he chose to work, but he'd been slacking off all term.

46
00:02:31.338 --> 00:02:34.779
"He's probably dreading the exam," Soames said.

47
00:02:34.799 --> 00:02:40.300
"And here's something else you might want to know: he was nearly expelled for cheating at cards during

48
00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.681
his first year at the college."

49
00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:44.581
"So you think McLaren is the most likely suspect?"

50
00:02:45.162 --> 00:02:45.642
Holmes said.

51
00:02:46.222 --> 00:02:48.162
Soames' hands fluttered in protest.

52
00:02:48.182 --> 00:02:50.343
"I wouldn't want to accuse anyone.

53
00:02:51.063 --> 00:02:53.404
But McLaren is probably the one most likely to cheat."

54
00:02:54.228 --> 00:02:58.049
As we approached Soames' rooms, Holmes stood on his tiptoes and looked through the window.

55
00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:01.930
"You'll notice that the window has many small panes," Soames said.

56
00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:06.891
"There's no way anyone could fit through those spaces, so the culprit must have used the door."

57
00:03:08.772 --> 00:03:13.473
Holmes raised his eyebrows at me, and I had to hide a smile at Soames' observation, which was

58
00:03:13.553 --> 00:03:15.434
so obvious to the great detective and me.

59
00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:20.655
As there was nothing more to be learned outside, we went into the building, and Soames unlocked his

60
00:03:20.695 --> 00:03:25.349
door. While Holmes examined the sitting room, the two of us waited in the doorway.

61
00:03:25.369 --> 00:03:27.970
"There are no footprints on the carpet," Holmes said.

62
00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:31.031
"But I didn't think I'd find any on such a dry day.

63
00:03:31.851 --> 00:03:33.812
Now, where did you leave your servant?"

64
00:03:34.573 --> 00:03:36.193
"Bannister was sitting in my desk chair."

65
00:03:36.213 --> 00:03:40.035
"Interesting. Well, you can come in now that I've finished with the carpet."

66
00:03:40.795 --> 00:03:41.676
Holmes motioned to us.

67
00:03:41.696 --> 00:03:43.516
"I think I know what happened.

68
00:03:44.217 --> 00:03:47.898
The student took the pages one by one over to the small table by the window.

69
00:03:49.779 --> 00:03:52.120
"From there, he could watch the courtyard for your return.

70
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.361
Then he could make his escape before you found him in your rooms."

71
00:03:56.281 --> 00:04:01.163
"I hate to contradict you," Soames said, "but he couldn't see me in the courtyard because I entered

72
00:04:01.203 --> 00:04:02.044
through a side gate."

73
00:04:02.064 --> 00:04:05.125
"The student had no way of knowing that," Holmes snapped.

74
00:04:05.725 --> 00:04:08.546
"I think he took the first page over to the table and began copying it.

75
00:04:09.287 --> 00:04:10.387
Now, how long would that take?

76
00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:12.028
Maybe 15 minutes?

77
00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:15.109
Then he tossed it on the floor and picked up the next page.

78
00:04:15.849 --> 00:04:19.031
He was in the middle of that when your sudden return caused him to rush away."

79
00:04:19.051 --> 00:04:23.100
"And he didn't have time to put the two pages back on the desk," I said.

80
00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.742
"Very good, Watson."

81
00:04:26.523 --> 00:04:28.604
Holmes beamed as if I were his prize pupil.

82
00:04:28.624 --> 00:04:33.167
"But I didn't hear anyone running up the stairs as I entered," Soames protested.

83
00:04:33.948 --> 00:04:34.668
Holmes ignored him.

84
00:04:34.688 --> 00:04:39.512
"At any rate, he was writing so furiously that he broke his pencil and had to sharpen it.

85
00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:45.436
This pencil was unusual—dark blue with the manufacturer's name in silver lettering—and very short.

86
00:04:46.296 --> 00:04:47.657
Only a couple inches remained."

87
00:04:48.438 --> 00:04:49.519
Holmes held out a shaving.

88
00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:51.360
"Do you see what I mean, Soames?"

89
00:04:52.264 --> 00:04:54.226
"I'm afraid I don't," Soames said.

90
00:04:54.246 --> 00:04:59.770
Holmes gave an exasperated sigh and pointed to the letters NN with a space after them.

91
00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:04.433
"You are aware that Johann Faber is the most common manufacturer of pencils?

92
00:05:05.293 --> 00:05:08.876
This pencil was made by Faber—the Ns come from the first name Johann."

93
00:05:10.497 --> 00:05:13.239
Holmes raised his eyebrows at me again, but I said nothing.

94
00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:18.243
He examined the wood shavings on the little table and concluded that the student had used a large

95
00:05:18.343 --> 00:05:19.804
blunt knife to sharpen the pencil.

96
00:05:20.576 --> 00:05:24.178
Holmes moved over to the desk, where he picked up and examined a small black lump.

97
00:05:24.198 --> 00:05:26.840
"I assume this is the strange clay that you spoke of."

98
00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.522
Soames nodded, but Holmes was already studying the cut on the leather desktop.

99
00:05:32.443 --> 00:05:35.504
It began with a tiny scratch and ended in a jagged hole.

100
00:05:35.524 --> 00:05:37.225
"A most unusual cut."

101
00:05:38.046 --> 00:05:39.086
Holmes pointed to a door.

102
00:05:39.106 --> 00:05:40.707
"Now, where does this lead to?"

103
00:05:40.727 --> 00:05:42.928
"My bedroom," Soames said.

104
00:05:42.948 --> 00:05:46.750
"And have you been in there since you discovered someone had tampered with the proofs?"

105
00:05:46.771 --> 00:05:49.172
"No, I came straight to you."

106
00:05:51.064 --> 00:05:52.344
"Then I would like to have a look around."

107
00:05:53.385 --> 00:05:55.405
Holmes held out his arm to bar us from the room.

108
00:05:55.425 --> 00:05:58.286
"Please allow me to examine the floor before you enter."

109
00:05:59.146 --> 00:06:01.987
He looked all around the room but once again found no footprints.

110
00:06:02.007 --> 00:06:05.008
"I assume you hang your clothes behind this curtain."

111
00:06:05.528 --> 00:06:07.869
Holmes gestured toward a piece of fabric along one wall.

112
00:06:07.889 --> 00:06:11.990
"If anyone was forced to hide himself in this room, he'd do it there.

113
00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.331
The bed is too low, and the wardrobe is too shallow.

114
00:06:16.031 --> 00:06:17.932
Shall we see if anyone is hiding behind the curtain?"

115
00:06:18.676 --> 00:06:22.099
My heart began to pound as I noticed the wary look on Holmes' face.

116
00:06:22.859 --> 00:06:27.242
I knew that my friend fully expected to pull back the curtain and find the culprit still hiding

117
00:06:27.282 --> 00:06:27.502
there!
